    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0330" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg256"/>

                <head>Mr Bigelow to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April,</hi> 1865</date></dateline>.</opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I beg to enclose a translation of an
                    article which appeared in the Memorial Diplomatique of Saturday last, purporting
                    to give the basis of certain peace negotiations in progress in Canada, between
                    persons representing the united States and the confederate insurgents. The quasi
                    official character of this hebdomadal satisfies me that the government wish the
                    facts there stated to be believed. I was confirmed in this opinion when I saw
                    the article promptly reappear in all the official journals.</p>
                <p>1 am, sir, with great respect, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d395-a1.xml" xpointer="d395-a1"/>
            </div>
